-- title:
--   Geelen, Gerards, Kapoor: seven excluded minors for $\mathrm{GF}(4)$
-- statement:
--   **The excluded minors for quaternary matroids**, as the rung $S(4,7)$ of Challenge 2:
--
--   $$\text{for } q\in\{2,3,4\},\ \text{the class of } \mathrm{GF}(q)\text{-representable matroids has at most seven excluded minors up to isomorphism.}$$
--
--   Geelen, Gerards and Kapoor proved that $\mathrm{GF}(4)$ has exactly seven excluded minors; the bounds for $\mathrm{GF}(2)$ and $\mathrm{GF}(3)$ (one and four) are covered by the same number.
-- source:
--   J. F. Geelen, A. M. H. Gerards, A. Kapoor, The excluded minors for GF(4)-representable matroids, JCTB 79 (2000), 247–299, https://doi.org/10.1006/jctb.2000.1963, main theorem (Theorem 1.1)

